\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Language-addressable spline action programs.} A long-horizon instruction is scheduled as executable clauses. For each clause, the VLA predicts eight control points for a continuous path, a gripper curve, and event duration $T$, rather than a dense fixed-rate waypoint array. The matched experiment isolates an additional +9.33~pp clause benefit for the spline head; the same shape--time factorization supports successful decode-time retiming on CALVIN.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Language-addressable spline action programs.} A long-horizon instruction is scheduled as executable clauses. For each clause, the VLA predicts eight control points for a continuous path, a gripper curve, and event duration $T$, rather than a dense fixed-rate waypoint array. The matched experiment isolates an additional +9.33~pp clause benefit for the spline head; the same shape--time factorization supports successful decode-time retiming on CALVIN}{figure.1}{}}
